Subject: [PATCH] changeguard: pin to a real release (feed builds a 404 URL)

The kenzok8/jell changeguard Makefile sets
  PKG_VERSION:=kaiplus-runtime-v1.0.18
and derives both the release tag and the asset name from it, producing
  .../download/changeguard-runtime-vkaiplus-runtime-v1.0.18/
  changeguard-kaiplus-runtime-v1.0.18-$(ARCH).tar.gz
Neither exists on istoreos/istoreos-app-hub: the real releases are
tagged changeguard-runtime-v0.3.x and ship changeguard-0.3.x-$(ARCH).tar.gz
(top dir changeguard-0.3.x, containing changeguard_bin, which is exactly
what Package/changeguard/install consumes). Every mirror therefore returns
404 and the build aborts with:
  No more mirrors to try - giving up.

Pin PKG_VERSION to the latest real changeguard release (0.3.5). The
override is placed after include ./release.mk and before the first use
of $(PKG_VERSION), so PKG_SOURCE, PKG_SOURCE_URL and PKG_BUILD_DIR all
expand to 0.3.5. The feed's own PKG_VERSION line is left untouched, so
the hunk keeps applying across kaiplus-version bumps.

Applied to feeds/kenzok8 (jell).

--- a/feeds/kenzok8/changeguard/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/kenzok8/changeguard/Makefile
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@ PKG_NAME:=changeguard
 PKG_VERSION:=kaiplus-runtime-v1.0.18
 PKG_RELEASE:=1
 include ./release.mk
+# The feed derives the tag/asset from PKG_VERSION, but pins a kaiplus
+# version that has no changeguard release. Use the latest real changeguard
+# release instead; PKG_SOURCE/_URL below expand from this value.
+PKG_VERSION:=0.3.5
 PKG_SOURCE:=changeguard-$(PKG_VERSION)-$(ARCH).tar.gz
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://github.com/istoreos/istoreos-app-hub/releases/download/changeguard-runtime-v$(PKG_VERSION)/
 PKG_HASH:=skip
